lisa-design:
- Digest pinning is one rule for the whole dockerfile manager (matchManagers dockerfile, pinDigests true), not per image or per repo: every FROM gets pinned; internal ghcr.io/compliance-framework/** images stay off through the existing internal rule (enabled false), which this rule does not override.
- minimumReleaseAgeBehaviour timestamp-optional lives in a sibling rule scoped to matchDatasources docker + matchUpdateTypes digest/pinDigest, not on the dockerfile rule: image version updates (minor/patch/major) keep timestamp-required. Chosen over minimumReleaseAge null so a digest update that does have a timestamp still waits 7 days.
- Evidence (Renovate 44.145.1 --dry-run=lookup on api and ui): every docker update had releaseTimestamp null; pinDigest of golang:1.26 and node:22 were pendingChecks true without the sibling rule and not pending with it; pinDigest of unversioned tags (nginx:stable-alpine, distroless) skip the age check either way; digest updates of unversioned tags get no such skip (lookup/digest.js passes currentVersionWasResolved=true), so they would never branch without the rule.

lisa-selfreview:
